  "_comment": "WP-57 Hang: how Voice/tts/speakable() turns a terse answer into text a voice can say. Extend freely: `words` are whole tokens matched case-sensitively first, then case-insensitively; a capitalised word also matches with a Hungarian ending (Plannert, Plannerben → plennert, plennerben); `phrases` are matched before words (longest first); `letters` spell an all-caps acronym that is not in `words`; `symbols` replace single characters. Hungarian numbers are spelled out by code (0 … 999 999); English keeps digits (the English voice reads them).",
